========================================================================
FIXED BUILD at 1 MHz: every step must PASS
========================================================================
Steps 1-9 of 9; each ends with RETURN and shows PASS or FAIL.
Type ONLY while the '>' prompt shows (keys pressed while the program prints are lost).
NO joystick in control port 2 (it locks the keyboard out by design).
Do each step exactly as described: the driver checks HOW (held time, keys down
at once, which SHIFT, the stick's row).  A skipped step is never a pass.

STEP 1  HOLD Q
   do:     hold Q for 2 s, release it, press RETURN
   expect: the line 'q', then STEP 1 PASS
   defect: ^q: the UP-ARROW glyph ($5E, c6r6, read in the same sample as Q) then q; or nothing (the phantom keeps restarting the debounce)
STEP 2  HOLD ; AND /
   do:     hold ; for 2 s, release; hold / for 2 s, release; RETURN
   expect: the line ';/', then STEP 2 PASS
   defect: l; (c5r2, bleed from ;) or ,/ (c5r7, bleed from /)
STEP 3  ROLLOVER
   do:     press Z and keep it down, add I, add P (all three held), release all, RETURN
   expect: the line 'zip', then STEP 3 PASS
   defect: a missing or doubled letter, or a letter nobody pressed
STEP 4  RSHIFT, C=
   do:     hold RIGHT SHIFT: type A and /, release; hold C=: type Q, release; RETURN (do not touch LEFT SHIFT)
   expect: the line 'A?q', then STEP 4 PASS
   defect: a/ (RSHIFT not decoded), or an extra character from C=
STEP 5  PORT-1 STICK UP
   do:     hold the stick in CONTROL PORT 1 UP and type HOSE; release the stick; RETURN
   expect: the line 'hose', then STEP 5 PASS
   defect: 1 3 5 7 9 + \ appear (row 0), DEL rubs characters out
STEP 6  PORT-1 STICK DOWN
   do:     hold the stick in CONTROL PORT 1 DOWN and type HOSE; release the stick; RETURN
   expect: the line 'hose', then STEP 6 PASS
   defect: the step ends at once with an empty line (RETURN is on row 1): SKIP, then w r y i p * _ land in the next line
STEP 7  PORT-1 STICK LEFT
   do:     hold the stick in CONTROL PORT 1 LEFT and type HOSE; release the stick; RETURN
   expect: the line 'hose', then STEP 7 PASS
   defect: CTRL reads as held (row 2): letters turn into control codes, CTRL+D ends the program, CTRL+J ends the line; a d g j l ;
STEP 8  PORT-1 STICK RIGHT
   do:     hold the stick in CONTROL PORT 1 RIGHT and type HOSE; release the stick; RETURN
   expect: the line 'hose', then STEP 8 PASS
   defect: 4 6 8 0 - 2 appear (row 3)
